DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccddccoonnttrrooll utility is a program to control audio features of a CD
     drive.  The device is a name such as _c_d_0.

     If no _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is given, then ccddccoonnttrrooll enters an interactive mode, read‐
     ing commands from the standard input.

     The following options are available:

     --ss      Silent mode.  Do not print table headers and human readable com‐
             ments.

     --vv      Verbose mode.  Print as much information as possible.

     --ff _d_e_v_i_c_e
             Specify a device, such as _/_d_e_v_/_c_d_0.  Both absolute path and rela‐
             tive to _/_d_e_v filename are possible.  The --ff option overrides
             CDROM.  If neither CDROM nor the --ff option is specified,
             ccddccoonnttrrooll tries opening first _/_d_e_v_/_c_d_r_o_m, then _/_d_e_v_/_c_d_0.

     The available commands are listed below.  Only as many characters as are
     required to uniquely identify a command need be specified.  The word ppllaayy
     can be omitted or the characters ++ and -- can be used in the place of nneexxtt
     and pprreevv.

     ppllaayy _f_i_r_s_t___t_r_a_c_k [_l_a_s_t___t_r_a_c_k]
             Play from track _f_i_r_s_t___t_r_a_c_k to track _l_a_s_t___t_r_a_c_k.  The first track
             has number 1.  Can be omitted in all cases.

     ppllaayy _s_t_a_r_t___m:_s_t_a_r_t___s._s_t_a_r_t___f [_e_n_d___m:_e_n_d___s._e_n_d___f]
             Play from the absolute address (MSF) defined by _s_t_a_r_t___m in min‐
             utes, _s_t_a_r_t___s, in seconds and _s_t_a_r_t___f (frame number) to the abso‐
             lute address defined by _e_n_d___m in minutes, _e_n_d___s, in seconds and
             _e_n_d___f (frame number).  Minutes are in the range 0-99.  Seconds
             are in the range 0-59.  Frame numbers are in the range 0-74.

     ppllaayy [#_s_t_a_r_t___b_l_o_c_k [_l_e_n_g_t_h]]
             Play starting from the logical block _s_t_a_r_t___b_l_o_c_k using _l_e_n_g_t_h
             logical blocks.

     nneexxtt [_t_r_a_c_k_s]
             Skip forward a number of tracks (default 1).

     pprreevv [_t_r_a_c_k_s]
             Skip backward a number of tracks (default 1).

     ppaauussee   Stop playing.  Do not stop the disc.

     rreessuummee  Resume playing.  Used after the ppaauussee command.

     ssttoopp    Stop the disc.

     eejjeecctt   Eject the disc.

     cclloossee   Inject the disc.

     vvoolluummee  Same as _s_t_a_t_u_s _v_o_l_u_m_e command.

     vvoolluummee _l_e_v_e_l
